  {
   "id": "s25",
   "text": "This is the habit that separates beginners from people who ship.",
   "visual": [
    {
     "type": "hookcard",
     "theme": "obsidian",
     "text": "The habit that separates beginners from shippers",
     "accent": [
      "habit"
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s26",
   "text": "Before you change anything, read the output of the node before the problem. Most mistakes are not clever. A field is empty, a connection is missing, or the wrong thing was passed in. Check what went in, check what came out, then change one thing at a time. If you change three things at once, you will never know which one fixed it.",
   "visual": [
    {
     "type": "tiltedagentstage",
     "theme": "studio",
     "headline": "Read Before You Change",
     "accent": [
      "Read"
     ],
     "steps": [
      {
       "label": "Read previous node",
       "active": true
      },
      {
       "label": "Check input",
       "active": false
      },
      {
       "label": "Check output",
       "active": false
      },
      {
       "label": "Change one thing",
       "active": false
      }
     ],
     "output": {
      "title": "LIVE REASONING",
      "lines": [
       "Most mistakes are not clever",
       "Check what went in, what came out",
       "Change one thing at a time"
      ]
     },
     "focus": [
      "left",
      "center",
      "right",
      "center"
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "hookcard",
     "theme": "obsidian",
     "text": "Change three things at once? You'll never know which one fixed it.",
     "accent": [
      "three"
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "interactiveuicard",
     "theme": "sand",
     "headline": "Usual suspects",
     "kind": "checklist",
     "accent": [
      "suspects"
     ],
     "kicker": "CHECK FIRST",
     "items": [
      {
       "text": "Field empty?"
      },
      {
       "text": "Connection missing?"
      },
      {
       "text": "Wrong data passed in?"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s27",
   "text": "When something breaks, it breaks in one node, and n8n shows you which one.",
   "visual": [
    {
     "type": "hookcard",
     "theme": "studio",
     "text": "It breaks in one node",
     "accent": [
      "one",
      "node"
     ],
     "sub": "n8n shows you which."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s28",
   "text": "A red node means open it and read the error. Start with the basics: credentials, missing connections, and empty fields. Fix one thing, run it again, and watch the output change.",
   "visual": [
    {
     "type": "interactiveuicard",
     "theme": "sand",
     "headline": "Red node checklist",
     "kind": "checklist",
     "accent": [
      "Red"
