   "chapter": "Make it run on its own"
  },
  {
   "id": "s34",
   "text": "Two details here save you from a very annoying surprise.",
   "visual": [
    {
     "type": "hookcard",
     "theme": "obsidian",
     "text": "Two details save you",
     "accent": [
      "Two",
      "details"
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s35",
   "text": "First, check the timezone, because a nine in the morning schedule means nothing if the workflow thinks it is somewhere else. Second, use a cron expression when the preset options are not enough. For example, zero nine star star star means every day at nine, and star slash fifteen means every fifteen minutes. The guide has a cheat sheet.",
   "visual": [
    {
     "type": "interactiveuicard",
     "theme": "studio",
     "headline": "Check the timezone",
     "kind": "dropdown",
     "accent": [
      "timezone"
     ],
     "kicker": "DETAIL 1",
     "dropdown": {
      "label": "Timezone",
      "options": [
       "Workflow timezone",
       "Instance timezone"
      ],
      "picked": 0
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "interactiveuicard",
     "theme": "obsidian",
     "headline": "Cron: every day at nine",
     "kind": "typing",
     "accent": [
      "nine"
     ],
     "kicker": "DETAIL 2",
     "query": "0 9 * * *",
     "typing": "0 9 * * *"
    },
    {
     "type": "interactiveuicard",
     "theme": "sand",
     "headline": "Cron: every 15 minutes",
     "kind": "typing",
     "accent": [
      "15"
     ],
     "kicker": "CRON",
     "query": "*/15 * * * *",
     "typing": "*/15 * * * *"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s36",
   "text": "But a schedule does nothing until you do one last thing.",
